<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Assietta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1747</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Assietta · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Assietta was fought on 19 July 1747 on the Assietta ridge in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cottian-alps">Cottian Alps</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>. Piedmontese and Austrian troops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-iii-of-sardinia">Charles Emmanuel III of Sardinia</a>, entrenched on the heights, repulsed a much larger French army under the chevalier de Belle-Isle, who was killed. The victory protected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> from invasion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-assietta.jpg" alt="Battle of Assietta" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maitland Furmeyer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_mort_du_chevalier_de_Belle-Isle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
